-**Randomizer → Upgrades** uses one rule pane with matching add/edit/remove glyphs, automatically saved notes, a run button, default-hidden detailed logs and region completion messages. Fresh rule files receive the implemented rule notes; existing custom notes and intentional empty lists remain intact. Editing rule prose does not change the algorithm. Logs report seed/counts without revealing replacement identities. **Randomizer → Map upgrades** reads original level-SSO pickup settings and shows compatible truck names first, one upgrade column in new (original) format, types, source zone and change state. Hover Compatible trucks for a two-column comparison of the new and original upgrades and their compatible truck names. Region tiles, column sorting/filtering and details match Map trucks. Reset selected covers all visible filtered rows, reset regions covers selected regions independently of column filters, and reset all covers the loaded catalog. These actions remove preview assignments only. Reload refreshes sources; changed truck/ownership/progression inputs mark saved previews stale for explicit rerandomization. The source row identifies initial-PAK level settings; map-folder selection stays in Map trucks. **Upgrade Stage/Apply is disabled in this trial.** No XML, SSO, map archive or installed game file is changed by randomizing/resetting upgrades; trial previews are not added to Start's staged changes.
