+
+**Start → Apply pending PAK edits** writes the staged level-SSO reward strings and component XML exploration flags to the sparse updated overlay. Upgrade edits appear in Start even after restarting; later draft/reset changes do not alter the staged snapshot until staged again. Every target is checked before any upgrade file is written. Changed pickup sets, conflicting reward IDs or conflicting flag values reject Apply and retain the staged snapshot; unrelated XML/SSO edits are preserved. Only the exact source + zone + reward index and named component variant are patched. Original files, zone IDs, map scenes, rank/objective locks and installed archives are preserved. Pack to a new PAK using the existing workflow after applying. Runtime collection and already-collected zones in existing saves still require in-game verification.
 
 **Start → PAK** groups truck XML changes into one brief row per truck and state, using the localized truck name. The summary shows up to three readable field/value changes (for example fuel capacity, price, unlock rank, engine or winch compatibility), followed by a count of further changes. Hover for every original field, before/after value and source path. Pending and applied summaries retain their distinct colors. Rank XP, shared engine/winch definitions, addon files and other general edits remain separate entries. Grouping affects display only; Apply and pending counts still use the full underlying edit list.
 
